Tine to go to school again;


Holidays done!
Come, boys, can't complain;


Had a jolly run.
Come, boys; states and books;


Study now, like fun;
Merry faces pleasant looks;


Glad schools begunP
Good clothes to wear to school,


Warranted to wear;
(Now the days are getting cooD;


Won't split nor tear.
All the boys that we know


ASK their fathers all,
Please to hurry up and go


TO GREAT BROWN HALL.
Hurry up, parents; don't be slow Johnny and
Jack, and Jim and Joe, every respectable father
knows, need good strong school clothes. Clothes
that strong, clothes that stout that will last
you long, before wearing out.
Come, bring the youngsters one and ALL and wen
rig them out CHEAP,

